Package: emoxidize
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, dconf
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-emoxidize | gnome-shell
Description: single-instance GTK4 emoji picker
 Emoxidize is a fast, single-instance emoji picker built with GTK4 and
 libadwaita. It presents a searchable grid of all canonical Unicode
 emojis grouped into Recents, Smileys, People, Animals, Food, Travel,
 Activities, Objects, Symbols and Flags, with live search over CLDR
 names and keywords, skin-tone support (including showing all tones at
 once) and a configurable grid.
 .
 Selecting an emoji copies it to the clipboard; with the optional GNOME
 Shell paste bridge installed, pasting into the focused window is
 supported natively.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-emoxidize
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, gnome-shell (>= 45)
Description: GNOME Shell paste bridge for Emoxidize
 D-Bus paste bridge: receives the selected emoji from Emoxidize and
 pastes it into the focused window via the Mutter clipboard and a
 virtual keyboard Ctrl+V. Enables the "Paste automatically" feature of
 the Emoxidize picker.
